id: pm-rust-orientation-stale-evidence
title: Align native context idle evidence with the published settings and timestamps
description: Native context still reads stale_in_progress_hours as an integer JSON token and parses idle history timestamps as RFC 3339 only. The pinned pm-cli accepts integral decimal and exponent notation and interprets date-only stored evidence at UTC midnight. Reuse the claim activity semantics and add a pinned-oracle context case for both inputs.
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: follow-up,oracle,orientation
created_at: "2026-11-20T06:08:40.405Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-20T10:17:10.197Z"
author: codex-sol
parent: pm-rust-oracle-1118
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-20T10:17:06.200Z",codex-sol,"Round EV threads PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs655AhE and PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs655AhH are addressed by sharing the stored activity timestamp parser and the whole-hour settings decoder with claim evidence. The pinned context differential passes for substantive date-only history and the 24, 24.0 and 24e0 forms. The separate RFC 3339 context evaluation clock is still enforced."
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  tests/orientation_differential.rs,project,Date-only history and integral threshold parity
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  PM_RUST_REQUIRE_PUBLISHED_CLI=1 cargo test --locked --all-features --test orientation_differential context_idle_activity_and_threshold_match_oracle,project,codex-sol,"2026-11-20T10:17:09.907Z",local_mutation,fix/oracle-pm-cli-1118
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  docs/NATIVE_ORIENTATION.md,project,Native context and published orientation evidence
